{"text":"In fact, countries like Taiwan, Singapore, Chile, not just China, have shown that actually it's economic growth that is a prerequisite for democracy. In a recent study, the evidence has shown that income is the greatest determinant of how long a democracy can last. The study found that if your per capita income is about $1,000 a year, your democracy will last for about eight and a half years. If your per capita income is between $2,000 and $4,000 per year, then you're likely to only get 33 years of democracy. And only if your per capita income is above $6,000 a year will you have democracy come hell or high water. What this is telling us is that we need to first establish a middle class that is able to hold the government accountable. But perhaps it's also telling us that we should be worried about going around the world and shoehorning democracy, because ultimately we run the risk of ending up with illiberal democracies, democracies that in some sense could be worse than the authoritarian governments that they seek to replace.","words":[{"text":"In","start":0.0,"end":0.78},{"text":"fact","start":0.78,"end":1.12,"punct":","},{"text":"countries","start":1.64,"end":1.8},{"text":"like","start":1.8,"end":2.08},{"text":"Taiwan","start":2.08,"end":2.62,"punct":","},{"text":"Singapore","start":3.14,"end":3.5,"punct":","},{"text":"Chile","start":4.1,"end":4.48,"punct":","},{"text":"not","start":4.96,"end":5.16},{"text":"just","start":5.16,"end":5.48},{"text":"China","start":5.48,"end":5.92,"punct":","},{"text":"have","start":6.2,"end":6.42},{"text":"shown","start":6.42,"end":6.78},{"text":"that","start":6.78,"end":7.06},{"text":"actually","start":7.06,"end":7.74},{"text":"it's","start":7.74,"end":8.16},{"text":"economic","start":8.16,"end":8.54},{"text":"growth","start":8.54,"end":9.1},{"text":"that","start":9.1,"end":9.62},{"text":"is","start":9.62,"end":9.76},{"text":"a","start":9.76,"end":9.88},{"text":"prerequisite","start":9.88,"end":10.28},{"text":"for","star